 "name": "mosasaurus",
 "description": "Mosasaurus hoffmannii (028), the Maastricht giant marine lizard: massive deep skull that tapers in a long triangle to a blunt conical tip, NO bony rostrum (unlike tylosaurus), robust jaws open with interlocking conical teeth (gape reads as a zig-zag in silhouette; neck slightly narrower than skull) with conical teeth (dark red mouth, no blood), long body with dark grey-green #3f5a5a back over mid #5a7a76 with lighter scale arcs, pale belly, four paddle flippers with digit lines, tail ending in a downturned crescent fluke. Mid-tone for chalky #6aaabf water; reads tilted. Facing right; anchor centre; x -520..520, y -130..150.",
